# Fixed defect 131's class, 2026-09-29, C's `do { ... } while (c)`. Symptom:
# the braces after `do` were read as the block they stand for, their `{`
# named once, and then `while (x < 3)` after the `}` was read as a loop of its
# own with no body, `missing_body` at the line below it: one habit, two
# messages. Cause: nothing asked where that `while` stands. A `while` on the
# line of the `}` that closes braces whose `{` a report names is their tail:
# its condition is read, and says its own mistakes, and where no body follows
# it none is asked for (`selfhost/parse/loop_habit.hero`).

function main()
    x: i64 @ 0

    do {  #~ expected_end_of_line
        x @ x + 1
    } while (x < 3)
    print(x)

    do {  #~ expected_end_of_line
        x @ x + 1
    } while (x < )  #~ expected_expression
    print(x)
